  "notes": "{薄|うす}める means to make a liquid less concentrated by adding water or another substance. Can also be used figuratively for weakening an impression or effect.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{薄|うす}まる→薄まる：14062_usumaru⟧ (intransitive — becomes diluted on its own)\n- Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧Y⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{薄|うす}める (dilute X with Y)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{薄|うす}めて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means 'is in the process of diluting' (ongoing action).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{薄|うす}める: to dilute with water\n- {薄|うす}めて⟦{使|つか}う→使う：00473_tsukau⟧: to use in diluted form\n- {薄|うす}めた⟦{液|えき}→液：02270_eki⟧: diluted solution\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{薄|うす}い→薄い：00764_usui⟧: thin, weak, light (base adjective)\n- ⟦{薄|うす}まる→薄まる：14062_usumaru⟧: to become diluted (intransitive pair)\n- ⟦{濃|こ}い→濃い：02344_koi⟧: thick, concentrated (opposite quality)",
